            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.619,
            0.447,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.4 OCCURRENCE OF METALS"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.648,
            0.723,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The earth’s crust is the major source of metals. Seawater also contains some soluble salts such as sodium chloride, magnesium chloride, etc. The elements or compounds, which occur naturally in the earth’s crust, are known as minerals. At some places, minerals contain a very high percentage of a particular metal and the metal can be profitably extracted from it. These minerals are called ores.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.761,
            0.376,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.4.1 Extraction of Metals"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.79,
            0.725,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt about the reactivity series of metals. Having this knowledge, you can easily understand how a metal is extracted from its ore. Some metals are found in the earth’s crust in the free state. Some are found in the form of their compounds. The metals at the bottom of the activity series are the least reactive. They are often found in a free",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.916,
            0.27,
            0.93
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals and Non-metals"
            }
          ]
        },
